 "youtube": {
  "title": "War of the Bucket: Did a Stolen Pail Really Start a War?",
  "description": "The War of the Bucket is one of history's strangest stories: Modena, in Italy, still keeps a plain oak bucket taken from Bologna in 1325. Legend says the stolen bucket started the war. The truth runs the other way. In November 1325 a Bolognese army of about 30,000 met Modena's 7,000 at the Battle of Zappolino and broke within hours. The Modenese chased them to Bologna's walls, held a victory horse race outside the gates, and took a bucket from a well as their trophy. Centuries later, Alessandro Tassoni's mock-epic poem \"La secchia rapita\" made it famous.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for history's strangest true stories. What is the oddest war trophy you have ever heard of? Tell us in the comments!\n\n#shorts #warofthebucket #stickstory",
